{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988352-use-of-bloodlines","id":988352,"title":"Use of bloodlines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-16T13:08:45-07:00","id":988352,"title":"Use of bloodlines","content":"So how common are bloodlines? Is it likely that there might be a handful in any given city?<br /> <br /> Right now I have one bloodline with two or three members (Tremere bloodline, still working out all the stuff about it), but that seems pretty lopsided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T13:29:54-07:00","id":988365,"title":"","content":"Well, 1e talked about Bloodlines as if they were extremely rare, like there might be one or two in a given city, maybe more in an especially large one. The core book even had a sidebar about combatting &quot;Bloodline Madness&quot; when the players all want to play characters of different Bloodlines. Then it proceeded to crank out book after book with dozens of Bloodline options. It was this really weird situation where they were giving you more awesome character customization options than you know what to do with (literally, some of the Bloodlines were so specific it was hard to come up with a concept beyond &quot;member of the [whatever] Bloodline&quot;,) but then chastised you for wanting to use them. In practice, everyone I ever played with ignored the whole &quot;Bloodlines are rare&quot; thing, and there was almost never a question of <i>if</i> a character should have a Bloodline, but <i>which</i> Bloodline they should be. My LARP troupe had a Morbus, a Malkavian, a Khaibit, a Child of Judass, a Melissidae, a Spina, one of those pirate Ventrue I can't remember the name of, one of those Mekhet from the Clan book with the crazy blood control powers, one of the one-eyed voodoo Ventrue that have the Keymaster's power from the second Matrix movie, an Erszabet, and at least two custom Bloodlines, and that's just the ones I <i>knew about</i> (some folks liked to keep their in-character secrets out-of-character too.)<br /> <br /> On the opposite end of the spectrum, 2e doesn't say anything about how common or how rare Bloodlines are, but there are, what, three that have been officially updated to 2e? My personal preference is that they be on the rare side - it should always be a question of <i>if</i>, not <i>which</i>. But, they also shouldn't be so rare that players feel discouraged from considering them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-16-2016, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:20:32-07:00","id":988392,"title":"","content":"Same here. The gazillion bloodlines in the supplements would suggest it's actually pretty rare to have a city without bloodlines. That said, the fact that joining a bloodline is a voluntary act would probably make this not that common either. From what I seem to remember, you are introduced into a bloodline and you have to make an effort to change your own blood (or something). So the question is also to know why someone would want to join. The most direct reason is the new powers I guess, but I imagine that's one of the least common, because there is also an extra weakness and the powers would have to be really appealing to justify the effort and risk. I'm thinking the most common reason is that some bloodlines either have a legacy or are a sign you're one of the cool kids. I seem to remember the Spina are pretty well regarded in the Invictus. Some, like the Csalad or the Architects of the Monolith are pretty much miniature covenants and have a specific agenda. I guess in some domains, joining a bloodline opens doors if that bloodline has some powerful people in it. That would depend on how cohesive the bloodline is. Architects probably only share their secrets with each other and you might want to be a Ventrue and try to join them if you want their support (whether they let you or not is another matter), but I doubt Morbus give much of a damn if someone wants to join the bloodline. Actually I don't really see why anyone would want to become a Morbus, except...<br /> <br /> The final reason and probably a close second, if not more prominent, than the second one, is if you didn't have a choice. Probably if your sire is a member and wants his childers to join as well. He blood bound you/tricked you/abused you into joining and you never really realized you had an alternative. Some of the more fucked up bloodlines are probably spread a little like that. I'm guessing most sane people wouldn't want to be a Morbus or a Macellarius if given a choice.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I imagine a number a visible bloodlines act as an odd sort of nobility inside their domain/covenant (probably distributed differently in the world). As such, I guess they wouldn't be so easy to join anyone could do it, but not rare either. They're more like a local flavor of kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:22:51-07:00","id":988444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988352-use-of-bloodlines?p=988365#post988365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the opposite end of the spectrum, 2e doesn't say anything about how common or how rare Bloodlines are, but there are, what, three that have been officially updated to 2e? My personal preference is that they be on the rare side - it should always be a question of <i>if</i>, not <i>which</i>. But, they also shouldn't be so rare that players feel discouraged from considering them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I am thinking they shouldn't be everywhere but I might have a few in Seattle. I am glad that everyone's not expected to be in a bloodline because that would be a ton more work, even with the homebrew conversions in the sticky. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm really glad for those, however, simply because having <i>something</i> if people go for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/988352-use-of-bloodlines?p=988392#post988392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, I imagine a number a visible bloodlines act as an odd sort of nobility inside their domain/covenant (probably distributed differently in the world). As such, I guess they wouldn't be so easy to join anyone could do it, but not rare either. They're more like a local flavor of kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, this explanation helps a lot with figuring out what I do want from bloodlines, which is definitely not omnipresence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:29:02-07:00","id":988454,"title":"","content":"My rule of thumb for a chronicle would be no fewer than 1-in-10 and no more than 1-in-5. Enough to give the clans and/or covenants in a domain some flavor, but not enough to shift innate identity in from &quot;clan&quot; to bloodline.&quot; So in a domain with 100 vampires, you would have between 10 and 20 Kindred who were members of a bloodline. <br /> <br /> Also, I think it makes sense if local members of a bloodline have some political unity: a lot of bloodlines have a history of loyalty to a covenant, after all. <br /> <br /> And correct me if I'm wrong, but didn't 2e change the requirement to join your sire's bloodline from 2 Blood Potency to 1? RAW, that means that you could have a freshly-awakened vampire who is automatically a member of the bloodline. That also seems to jive with how they are presented in the 1e books, despite the 2 BP requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:37:59-07:00","id":988462,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the requirement was lowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T08:58:46-07:00","id":989373,"title":"","content":"I usually have it so bloodlines the PCs are interested in joining are present in the city, but aren't that common otherwise, unless I find one interesting enough for a NPC that will get screen time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:27:17-07:00","id":989456,"title":"","content":"I kinda use the model where clan is nation and bloodline is region. Everyone is from a region if they belong to a nation, but some regions have stronger identities and the people declare allegiance to the area first. Some people might even strongly associate with weak region identities. Conversely, some assume such a pan-nationalistic view that region is dismissed as an unimportant triviality. So you have 100% bloodline prevalence but it is seen by most as less important than which clan you are from, unless it is so pronounced as to differentiate you.<br /> <br /> For example, I nearly always make my Venture a member of my custom Nicomachus bloodline. The bloodline is purely thematic for now, with no mechanical difference. As such, it is polite to notice the bloodline, as its members take pride in it, but most vampires just regard them as Venture, especially beyond earshot. Morbus on the other hand present functional difficulties and so, while most know they are [gangrel?], the morbus identity is factored in first.<br /> <br /> The difference this makes is that bloodline prominence is a matter of power, not ratios. If only the Nicomachus rule this city, this mechanically neutral Venture bloodline will be factored in and not dismissed as 'just another Venture.' Meanwhile, if the city is overrun with Morbus that nevertheless exercise diligence over their weakness and keep a low profile, they may just be treated as the same as their clan mates. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not sure how RAW or RAI this is though or how neat the conceit is but it makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}